1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,880
Your bank holds Aziza's account, and she sells shoes online.

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:08,904
But when her customers pay by card, the money goes to Payme and Click, not to you.

3
00:00:08,904 --> 00:00:13,023
With its own acquiring, your bank earns a commission on every payment.

4
00:00:13,023 --> 00:00:16,047
The rest stays in your bank too, as deposits.

5
00:00:16,047 --> 00:00:19,523
But what if a shell company with a fake director tries to get in?

6
00:00:19,523 --> 00:00:25,095
Before any store goes live, two bank employees check its documents and the sanctions lists.

7
00:00:25,095 --> 00:00:29,535
A website selling iPhones for fifty thousand soum can look completely real.

8
00:00:29,535 --> 00:00:33,428
A fraudulent or illegal website can't take payments through your bank.

9
00:00:33,428 --> 00:00:38,464
And what if an approved store suddenly starts sending dozens of suspicious payments?

10
00:00:38,464 --> 00:00:42,059
If anything slips through, your bank shuts it down in seconds.

11
00:00:42,059 --> 00:00:46,547
A hacker copies a real payment request and changes the amount to ten million.

12
00:00:46,547 --> 00:00:52,023
Every payment request is signed with the store's secret key, and works only once.

13
00:00:52,023 --> 00:00:57,202
A network glitch makes the store send the same payment twice, and the customer's phone buzzes.

14
00:00:57,202 --> 00:01:01,523
If a request is sent twice, the customer is still charged once.

15
00:01:01,523 --> 00:01:06,773
Now the store check goes dark, and a suspended store tries to sneak a payment through.

16
00:01:06,773 --> 00:01:09,035
When in doubt, your bank says no.

